WEBVTT

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:46.790
Hello. You've reached my
answering machine.

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:48.790
Leave a message.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.860
Three, two, one, go!

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:58.100
What are you thinking?

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.090
Hello? It's me, Sugihara Shie.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.980
It's been a while.

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:33.930
Hey, Elis...

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.820
I had to see you.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.210
Hagino?

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.860
Just kidding.

00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.260
Excuse the intrusion!

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Light Purple All Night Long

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.220
She's a little demon.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:18.150
So this is Elis and your love nest?

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:22.380
Hagino, what are you...

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.650
Hagino-senpai?

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:26.000
What? What's going on?

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.720
I haven't slept a wink.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.400
I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:34.900
I'll just be sleeping here. Don't mind me.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.330
You're staying here?

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:40.460
Maybe I'll start living here.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:43.030
Did something happen?

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.430
Well...

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:49.860
Hey!

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:50.870
Senpai!

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:56.180
I'm hungry...

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.520
This is delicious. This is
incredibly delicious!

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.350
Isn't it? Onii-chan's rice omelet
will bring tears to your eyes.

00:04:10.940 --> 00:04:13.590
Why are you eating too, Elis?

00:04:13.590 --> 00:04:16.170
I forgot to eat lunch.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.900
Didn't you hear me calling you?

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.750
What? Really?

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.880
I'm stuffed!

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.050
Thanks for the food.

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.490
So, what's wrong?

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.830
My deadline's tomorrow.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.410
Deadline?

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:44.630
For your novel?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:50.570
For a magazine serial. If I don't
send it in by Monday morning...

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.020
What if you don't?

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.000
I'll be in a lot of trouble.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.560
Trouble?

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:59.040
That's tomorrow. You've written
something, haven't you?

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.880
Not a single page, line, or word.

00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.320
What?

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.420
It's not like I haven't been working.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.000
I haven't slept or eaten since
yesterday morning.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:12.120
I've been thinking this whole time.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.560
But...

00:05:17.430 --> 00:05:19.200
You can't do it.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.870
Isn't it another love story?

00:05:20.870 --> 00:05:26.400
Yes. I wanted to try something
new this time...

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:30.610
so I thought I'd write it like a girl's diary.

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:31.310
A diary?

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.950
Yeah. Her diary chronicling the
events between meeting...

00:05:34.950 --> 00:05:36.980
and parting ways with a boy.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.280
Sounds interesting.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.700
Doesn't it? But if I'm writing a diary...

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:45.880
I've got to include all sorts of details
about how it feels to be in love.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:50.950
But I've only ever been on
that one date with you.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.110
Right.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.940
I don't know what to do.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.740
That's why you can't write?

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.380
I thought I might be able to write
if I had a change of scenery.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:09.180
Why'd you have to come here?

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:11.590
Do you think you can write?

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:13.190
I don't know.

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.030
You don't know?

00:06:15.030 --> 00:06:18.420
But won't you be in trouble if
you don't write something?

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:22.160
My editor's really scary.

00:06:23.230 --> 00:06:25.200
Is she that woman who chased us?

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.450
Sugihara Shie-san. She's my editor.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:32.270
Her charm's in her slanted
eyes and eyebrows.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:35.440
She did seem like a harsh person.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.540
She's more than just harsh.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.080
That woman's a devil! A devil editor!

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.850
Senpai? Are you all right?

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:53.420
Sorry for calling you out here
so suddenly on a Sunday.

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:54.380
Not at all.

00:06:54.380 --> 00:06:57.610
I'm glad to see you again.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:59.240
Cheers!

00:06:59.240 --> 00:07:00.800
Cheers!

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:06.070
Did something happen?

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.010
The deadline's tomorrow!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.950
Why are you wearing pajamas?

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:18.240
How else am I supposed to relax?

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.820
You're not supposed to be relaxing!

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.140
You're supposed to write!

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:25.160
Elis-chan, you're scaring me.
You're just like Shie-san.

00:07:25.160 --> 00:07:26.970
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:26.970 --> 00:07:28.720
Okay, okay.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.260
But Hagino, are you going to be okay?

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.960
Your deadline's tomorrow morning.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:40.400
You can't expect me to write
love stories every month.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.110
I guess not.

00:07:42.440 --> 00:07:46.040
But Shie-san insists I can.

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:49.460
I only say that because
I believe she can do it.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:50.580
Does that make sense?

00:07:50.580 --> 00:07:51.920
Yes...

00:07:52.210 --> 00:07:53.750
But when I force myself to write...

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:57.590
she always complains it's
too ordinary or stale!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:02.360
I wish she wouldn't say she can't write
because she has no experience.

00:08:02.360 --> 00:08:06.220
A writer should have the imagination to
write about things they haven't done.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:09.420
You can write science fiction even
if you haven't met aliens.

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:12.480
You can write historical dramas even
if you've never seen a samurai.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.490
That's what writers do!

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.810
Right...

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.700
If that's what she wants,
Shie-san should write!

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:27.080
I guess a writer should never
say that, though...

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.520
That does sound difficult.

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:32.800
I'm sick of love!

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:36.230
I don't want to write love stories.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:40.870
I like your romance novels,
Hagino-senpai.

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:44.430
Hey, Hagino. I think she says
those harsh things...

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.800
with your best interests in mind.

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:51.180
Hagino?

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:54.110
Hagino-senpai?

00:08:55.530 --> 00:08:56.550
She's asleep...

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:05.320
Senpai, you haven't changed.

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:08.740
You're always worrying about others.

00:09:08.740 --> 00:09:09.930
Who, me?

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:12.400
In college, when I was wondering

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:16.370
if I should go to Tokyo to
see the man I loved...

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:18.640
Oh, that's right.

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:22.200
You thought about it with me.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.910
Didn't I tell you to go and see him?

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:27.580
I ended up not going, though.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:30.380
In the end, you have to make
the final decision.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:33.180
But I was really happy.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:36.250
You gave me the strength I needed.

00:09:36.840 --> 00:09:42.360
You're probably giving that writer
the same encouragement, too.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.580
I certainly hope so.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:52.070
18 hours until the deadline...

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:57.990
She said she hadn't slept
since yesterday.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.780
But won't she be in trouble?

00:10:00.780 --> 00:10:02.810
This can't be good.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:06.420
Onii-chan.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:11.460
Let's come up with a story.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.740
What?

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:39.620
I want her to become a proper writer.

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:43.920
I only criticized her so harshly because
I thought she could do it!

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:49.360
I forgot you're a crying drunk.

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:51.530
Kiri, are you even listening?

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:53.330
I'm listening!

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:55.550
Who am I kidding? I'm a devil.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:11:00.270
I'll become the world's
most devilish editor!

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:03.080
Okay, okay!

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:05.340
Senpai?

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:06.580
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.440
Are you okay?

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:09.780
I'm fine.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:16.320
Kikyo-sensei?

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.460
Huh? What are you all doing here?

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:25.450
What about you? Are you on a date?

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:29.560
No, no. I'm here with a college friend.

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:30.620
A woman.

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:32.470
That's no fun.

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:33.870
What are you girls doing?

00:11:33.870 --> 00:11:35.670
We're going to Kamikura-sensei's house.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:36.580
What?

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.410
Hosen-san called us.

00:11:40.410 --> 00:11:41.910
She called you?

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:46.680
Hagino-san can't seem to write
her novel due tomorrow...

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.680
and came crying to Kamikura-sensei...

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:53.870
She said we should help.

00:11:53.870 --> 00:11:56.390
We received urgent calls.

00:11:59.330 --> 00:12:01.730
Well, we have to get going.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:03.990
Excuse us.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:09.940
Is Hagino-san the writer Senpai's
been talking about?

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:12.700
What am I going to do?

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:15.330
I guess there's nothing to do, but...

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:17.980
What am I going to do?

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:26.060
What's wrong?

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.470
It's nothing.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.790
Where is she?

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:33.680
She might be closer than you think.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:38.600
...and there you have it.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:40.880
Where is she?

00:12:47.760 --> 00:12:49.850
...and there you have it.

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:57.320
If we don't do something,
she'll be in deep trouble.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:59.370
This sounds interesting.

00:12:59.370 --> 00:13:02.310
I have received my parents'
permission to stay out...

00:13:02.310 --> 00:13:04.100
so let's work on this until morning.

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:08.280
I feel like I've become a writer.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:10.820
But can amateurs really do this?

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:12.140
Should we even be doing this?

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:14.340
It's an emergency!

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:19.880
Ultimately, I'm sure Hagino
will have to write it.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:26.070
I think we should come up
with ideas to inspire her.

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.320
Okay.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.010
Let's begin.

00:13:32.950 --> 00:13:34.260
One night during a blizzard...

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:37.450
In a small mountain hut...

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:40.990
A boy had come to ski...

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.820
With a high school girl...

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:46.970
And they froze to death.

00:13:46.970 --> 00:13:48.440
What?

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:50.070
What?

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:53.310
It's okay. It was our first try.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.600
Let's do it again.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.710
Okay.

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:58.630
One hundred years ago today...

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:02.100
At a park with a beautiful
view of a harbor...

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:06.350
A shepherd brought his lunch...

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:09.790
To eat with a federal secret agent...

00:14:11.110 --> 00:14:12.830
And they got lost and died.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.900
What? Another death?

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:19.070
What? It's dramatic.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:22.020
Okay, let's try it one more time.

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:26.770
Misaki, Tamaru, don't forget
it's a love story.

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:30.250
I'm not sure shepherds
or secret agents fit in.

00:14:30.250 --> 00:14:31.780
Okay.

00:14:31.780 --> 00:14:32.950
Sorry.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.650
Okay, let's try again.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.170
Are you drunk?

00:14:39.170 --> 00:14:40.780
Nope.

00:14:41.590 --> 00:14:44.340
We're almost there, Senpai.

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:46.280
Okay!

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.570
I wonder if she's finished writing.

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:51.270
The deadline!

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.390
Let's try it again.

00:14:53.390 --> 00:14:54.200
Okay!

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.770
On a crisp Monday morning...

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:00.280
In an endless green field...

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:01.980
Good start.

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.740
An older brother...

00:15:04.640 --> 00:15:05.650
And his younger sister...

00:15:06.360 --> 00:15:08.650
Died while calling each other's names.

00:15:08.650 --> 00:15:10.530
What?

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:13.310
Tomoko-chan, why do they
always have to die?

00:15:13.310 --> 00:15:15.790
Can't you come up with a happy ending?

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.600
Isn't that what's good about
it? It'll make you cry.

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.310
I guess you're right.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:22.590
We could write a tragedy.

00:15:22.590 --> 00:15:26.190
I don't know about a tragic
love story, though.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.610
We can't work with a brother and sister.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.440
What would you prefer?

00:15:31.850 --> 00:15:35.810
Two cousins died while calling
each other's names.

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:40.820
That's definitely not okay!

00:15:50.730 --> 00:15:57.170
I had even bought an airplane ticket,
but couldn't go to see Hiroki...

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:59.970
What happened with with that guy?

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:05.480
I met him again recently.

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:09.450
Make sure you don't have
any regrets this time.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:10.530
Okay.

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:21.230
The deadline!

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:32.070
What is this? What are
they all doing here?

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:36.610
We've been trying to help you
with your novel, but...

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:43.550
We couldn't come up
with anything useful.

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:51.350
Elis-chan, Mami-senpai, Sumire-senpai...

00:16:51.350 --> 00:16:53.690
Hikari-chan, Tomoko-chan...

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:00.760
Sensei.

00:17:01.110 --> 00:17:02.470
What?

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:05.270
Love is amazing!

00:17:05.270 --> 00:17:06.200
What?

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.970
I really want to write!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.000
Really?

00:17:15.470 --> 00:17:17.210
You've still got six hours.

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:18.520
Yeah!

00:17:30.260 --> 00:17:32.230
Hagino, coffee.

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:01.020
She's only got five more hours.

00:18:07.280 --> 00:18:10.170
It's okay. She can do it.

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:36.460
File sent.

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:49.170
Looks like you made it on time.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.000
Here.

00:18:50.000 --> 00:18:51.710
Thank you.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:54.580
That smells delicious.

00:18:54.580 --> 00:18:55.980
Thanks.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:03.190
I managed to write something
incredible.

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:07.430
It might be Nakano Giwa's
greatest work!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:08.930
What'd you end up writing?

00:19:09.140 --> 00:19:12.360
A couple who spend an unbelievably
romantic night together...

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:15.730
have their morning coffee side
by side at the window sill!

00:19:16.670 --> 00:19:18.200
What kind of story is that?

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:21.870
Buy it and read it later!

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:25.310
I look forward to it.

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:29.360
I get a lot of work done here.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:31.570
You're going to come back?

00:19:31.570 --> 00:19:33.600
It's the perfect place for me to work.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:35.320
Give me a break!

00:19:36.240 --> 00:19:38.960
I'm glad you finished on time.

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:41.480
Don't you think I worked really hard?

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:43.020
Yeah, you did.

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:44.270
Then where's my reward?

00:19:44.270 --> 00:19:45.100
What?

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.600
Just kidding.

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:54.910
Onii-chan, you jerk!

00:20:24.160 --> 00:20:25.340
Shie-san...

00:20:25.340 --> 00:20:26.870
The devil?

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:34.740
I read it.

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:36.180
And?

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:39.880
It was interesting. I was moved.

00:20:48.880 --> 00:20:52.380
I look forward to your next submission.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.580
What?

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:01.350
Kiri-sensei.

00:21:03.050 --> 00:21:04.340
Good morning.

00:21:04.560 --> 00:21:05.910
Good morning.

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:12.220
What?

00:21:19.090 --> 00:21:21.220
What? What's going on?

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:26.870
Hey, Kiri!

00:23:11.890 --> 00:23:13.800
Cherry pink is the color of blush.

00:23:14.180 --> 00:23:17.670
The color of a girl's cheeks.

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:19.170
Hey, Hiroki...

00:23:19.170 --> 00:23:23.200
It seems those girls who seem strong
at first but later become warm...

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:26.550
the so-called tsundere, are
quite popular these days.

00:23:26.550 --> 00:23:27.680
Of course they are.

